   "notes": "The primary table reports formula-molar MgSiO3 volume. Parenthesized last-digit volume uncertainties are preserved, but the paper does not identify their confidence convention. The pressure footnote says that pressures were determined from the Jamieson et al. (1982) Pt EOS and points with error greater than 0.5 GPa were rejected; no retained-row pressure errors or Pt observations are tabulated. Thermocouple errors are stated to be less than +/-10 K, without row-specific values or a confidence convention. Ten rows are at 300 K; only those rows directly benchmark the executable static slice. The full published thermal analysis also used earlier literature data that are not reprinted in this article.",
